1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:07,576
This is the booking assistant, running live. Chat mode — and
the guest opens with almost nothing.

2
00:00:07,576 --> 00:00:10,288
Just: we would like to book a room.

3
00:00:20,736 --> 00:00:27,432
So the assistant asks for what it does not have yet — the
date, the nights, how many guests, a name.

4
00:00:27,432 --> 00:00:29,376
The guest adds two of them.

5
00:00:29,376 --> 00:00:33,576
Two people, from October seventeenth, for three nights.

6
00:00:50,201 --> 00:00:59,321
Now it can work out the check-out, the room and the meal plan
itself. Only two things are still missing: diving, and a name.

7
00:00:59,321 --> 00:01:01,385
Yes to diving, one room.

8
00:01:01,385 --> 00:01:06,353
Notice the room count is one — the guest's own answer, not a
guess.

9
00:01:29,367 --> 00:01:31,239
One left.

10
00:01:31,239 --> 00:01:33,855
A name, and the airport pickup.

11
00:01:33,855 --> 00:01:38,727
That answer also settles the transfer, so nothing more is
owed.

12
00:01:53,765 --> 00:02:02,573
Four turns, and the enquiry is complete — every figure read
back, and it never asked twice for anything the guest had
already said.

13
00:02:02,573 --> 00:02:04,283
Now the other mode.

14
00:02:04,283 --> 00:02:05,867
Single message — three cases in a row.

15
00:02:05,867 --> 00:02:09,875
Case one: three guests, two of them divers.

16
00:02:12,480 --> 00:02:15,576
Extract reads the whole message at once.

17
00:02:23,670 --> 00:02:28,950
Every field filled, each with the exact words the guest used
as evidence.

18
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:37,462
Case two.

19
00:02:37,462 --> 00:02:44,926
A dive club: ten guests, five rooms, and a split schedule —
six people dive four days, four dive two.

20
00:02:48,864 --> 00:02:53,328
Plus a partner rate request, which is not the assistant's to
answer.

21
00:02:58,985 --> 00:03:05,153
The split schedule is kept whole, and the partner rate is
routed to the reservations team.

22
00:03:11,786 --> 00:03:13,658
Case three.

23
00:03:13,658 --> 00:03:16,922
A family of four, where only two dive.

24
00:03:20,416 --> 00:03:25,936
Guest count and diver count are different numbers, and the
dive line is priced per head.

25
00:03:34,184 --> 00:03:39,032
Four guests, two divers, and the two children noted as
snorkelling.

26
00:03:39,032 --> 00:03:47,280
Both modes end the same way: nothing is booked, and no price
is quoted. The assistant handles the conversation; your team
makes every call about money.
